#N canvas 0 50 1040 1060 12;
#X text 30 16 =^..^=   grain~   version 1 (2026)   sofia vallejo budziszewski   iem kug graz austria;
#X text 30 46 pitch-aware granulator;
#X text 30 86 a granulator that listens to the pitch of its input. grains can be cut to whole periods of the sound and retuned to the nearest note of a scale. grains can play backwards with a probability and the read position can be scrubbed by data, f 110;
#X text 30 166 --- how it was made ---;
#X text 30 210 a four second ring buffer is read by up to 64 overlapping grains. the pitch of the input is tracked with a yin style difference function every 256 samples. grains use cubic interpolation and a window that goes from hann to almost rectangular, f 110;
#X text 30 290 --- how to use ---;
#X text 30 334 1  open the engine page and switch the sound on, f 110;
#X text 30 364 2  load a preset and listen. size and density set the texture, f 110;
#X text 30 394 3  turn tune to 1 with a scale to pull every grain to the nearest scale note of the detected pitch, f 110;
#X text 30 424 4  move scrub or map data to it to read the past of the sound, f 110;
#X text 30 454 everything is a message: see the messages page for the full list and the examples page for patches to copy. every effect has presets and a and b morph and mutate and a data inlet, f 110;
#X text 30 514 try:  sync on makes grains start on period boundaries so tones stay clean, f 110;
#X text 30 544 try:  the pitch outlet sends pitch hz confidence about twenty times per second, f 110;
#X text 30 574 try:  reverse 0.3 with spray gives a cloud that sometimes runs backwards, f 110;
#X text 30 618 --- common problems ---;
#X text 30 662 no sound: the buffer must fill first. scrub 0 reads the present and needs some input, f 110;
#X text 30 692 tune has no effect: the input must have a clear pitch. watch the pitch outlet, f 110;
#X text 30 722 grains sound rough: turn sync on or raise the grain size, f 110;
#X text 30 752 names: give every instance its own name as the first argument like [tessera/grain~ g1]. the name is also the stash namespace, f 110;
#X text 30 816 --- click a box to open that page ---;
#N canvas 0 50 900 1134 presets 0;
#X text 30 16 factory sounds are stored as plain text. click a box to load that sound. every slider in the effect follows, f 100;
#X text 30 66 --- factory presets ---;
#X msg 30 110 \; g1 preset 0;
#X text 240 112 0  default;
#X msg 30 164 \; g1 preset 1;
#X text 240 166 1  cloud;
#X msg 30 218 \; g1 preset 2;
#X text 240 220 2  pitch snap;
#X msg 30 272 \; g1 preset 3;
#X text 240 274 3  frozen glass;
#X msg 30 326 \; g1 preset 4;
#X text 240 328 4  reverse wash;
#X msg 460 110 \; g1 preset 5;
#X text 670 112 5  octave swarm;
#X msg 460 164 \; g1 preset 6;
#X text 670 166 6  choir sync;
#X msg 460 218 \; g1 preset 7;
#X text 670 220 7  dust;
#X msg 460 272 \; g1 preset 8;
#X text 670 274 8  slow scan;
#X text 30 400 --- now playing ---;
#X symbolatom 30 444 20 0 0 0 - g1-name -;
#X floatatom 230 444 4 0 0 0 - g1-index -;
#X text 340 446 name and number (minus one means edited);
#X msg 30 488 \; g1 next;
#X msg 142 488 \; g1 prev;
#X msg 254 488 \; g1 mutate 0.3;
#X text 30 548 next and prev step through the presets and wrap around. mutate varies the current sound by a random amount from 0 to 1. mutate leaves mix and level alone, f 100;
#X text 30 598 --- morph between two sounds ---;
#X msg 30 642 \; g1 A;
#X msg 118 642 \; g1 B;
#X text 206 644 a and b remember the current sound;
#X text 30 704 morph;
#X obj 110 702 hsl 300 18 0 1 0 0 g1-morph empty empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 30 746 load one preset and press a then load another and press b then move the morph slider. every continuous parameter blends smoothly. switches change at the middle, f 100;
#X text 30 796 --- your own user bank ---;
#X msg 30 840 \; g1 store mysound;
#X msg 214 840 \; g1 save my.bank;
#X msg 390 840 \; g1 load my.bank;
#X text 30 900 store keeps the current sound after the factory presets. save writes the user bank to a text file next to this patch and load reads such a file, f 100;
#X text 30 950 --- presets with stash ---;
#X text 30 994 every slider of the effect sends to g1-param and listens on g1-param-r. this is the naming scheme of the stash preset library: create [stash/bank g1] and send it a scan message with the name of the patch that holds the effect. it follows the stash rules but has not been tested together yet, f 100;
#X restore 30 860 pd presets;
#X text 30 894 all sounds and morph, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1200 1022 parameters 0;
#X text 30 16 every parameter is also a message: [name value( in real units or for a switch the option name or number. the controls in the effect panel and these messages do the same, f 120;
#X text 30 66 parameter;
#X text 210 66 values;
#X text 560 66 what it does;
#X text 30 100 size;
#X text 210 100 5 to 500 log, f 36;
#X text 560 100 grain length in ms (with sync on it is rounded to whole periods), f 54;
#X text 30 156 density;
#X text 210 156 1 to 200 log, f 36;
#X text 560 156 grains per second, f 54;
#X text 30 192 scrub;
#X text 210 192 0 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 192 read position in the past. 0 is now and 1 is about four seconds ago, f 54;
#X text 30 248 spray;
#X text 210 248 0 to 500, f 36;
#X text 560 248 random extra delay of the read position in ms, f 54;
#X text 30 284 pitch;
#X text 210 284 -24 to 24, f 36;
#X text 560 284 transposition of every grain in semitones, f 54;
#X text 30 320 tune;
#X text 210 320 0 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 320 how strongly grains are pulled to the nearest scale note of the detected pitch, f 54;
#X text 30 376 key;
#X text 210 376 c | c# | d | d# | e | f | f# | g | g# | a | a# | b, f 36;
#X text 560 376 root of the scale for tune, f 54;
#X text 30 432 scale;
#X text 210 432 chromatic | major | minor | pentatonic | whole | dorian | fifths, f 36;
#X text 560 432 scale for tune, f 54;
#X text 30 508 scatter;
#X text 210 508 0 to 12, f 36;
#X text 560 508 random pitch per grain in semitones, f 54;
#X text 30 544 reverse;
#X text 210 544 0 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 544 probability that a grain plays backwards, f 54;
#X text 30 580 sync;
#X text 210 580 off | on, f 36;
#X text 560 580 on cuts grains to whole periods and starts them on period boundaries, f 54;
#X text 30 636 shape;
#X text 210 636 0 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 636 0 averages over time and 1 holds the loudest moments, f 54;
#X text 30 692 spread;
#X text 210 692 0 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 692 stereo spread of the grains, f 54;
#X text 30 728 jitter;
#X text 210 728 0 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 728 random phase of every frame. 0 is a pure drone and higher is airier, f 54;
#X text 30 784 freeze;
#X text 210 784 off | on, f 36;
#X text 560 784 on stops writing to the buffer so the grains keep reading the same sound, f 54;
#X text 30 840 mix;
#X text 210 840 0 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 840 0 is the dry sound and 1 is only grains, f 54;
#X text 30 876 gain;
#X text 210 876 -24 to 12, f 36;
#X text 560 876 output gain in db, f 54;
#X text 30 922 any continuous parameter can be driven by data: send datamap name amount and then data 0 to 1. see the messages page, f 120;
#X restore 220 860 pd parameters;
#X text 220 894 every control, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1300 980 messages 0;
#X text 30 16 click any box to send it to the effect. the effect listens to its name so you can use [s g1] from anywhere in your patch, f 110;
#X text 30 66 message;
#X text 430 66 what it does;
#X msg 30 100 \; g1 params;
#X text 430 102 prints every parameter and its range in the console, f 76;
#X msg 30 154 \; g1 preset 3;
#X text 430 156 loads preset 3 (or a preset by name: preset cloud), f 76;
#X msg 30 208 \; g1 next;
#X text 430 210 next preset (wraps around), f 76;
#X msg 30 262 \; g1 prev;
#X text 430 264 previous preset, f 76;
#X msg 30 316 \; g1 mutate 0.4;
#X text 430 318 random variation of the current sound. 0 is nothing and 1 is a lot, f 76;
#X msg 30 370 \; g1 A;
#X text 430 372 remember the current sound as a, f 76;
#X msg 30 424 \; g1 B;
#X text 430 426 remember the current sound as b, f 76;
#X msg 30 478 \; g1 morph 0.5;
#X text 430 480 blend between a and b from 0 to 1, f 76;
#X msg 30 532 \; g1 data 0.7;
#X text 430 534 data inlet: a value from 0 to 1, f 76;
#X msg 30 586 \; g1 datamap scrub 0.5;
#X text 430 588 map the data inlet to a continuous parameter. 0.5 means the full range of the parameter at data 0 and 1. amount 0 removes the mapping. up to four mappings, f 76;
#X msg 30 660 \; g1 datamap clear;
#X text 430 662 remove all data mappings, f 76;
#X msg 30 714 \; g1 store mysound;
#X text 430 716 keep the current sound in the user bank, f 76;
#X msg 30 768 \; g1 save my.bank;
#X text 430 770 write the user bank to a text file, f 76;
#X msg 30 822 \; g1 load my.bank;
#X text 430 824 read a user bank, f 76;
#X msg 30 876 \; g1 pitch;
#X text 430 878 the pitch outlet sends pitch hz confidence about twenty times per second while dsp is on, f 76;
#X restore 410 860 pd messages;
#X text 410 894 clickable list, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1300 1000 examples 0;
#X text 30 16 copy these into your own patch. they all talk to the effect through [s g1] so the engine page must be open with dsp on, f 130;
